      "definition": "(G) As used in this section, \"actual economic damages\" means damages for direct, incidental, or consequential pecuniary losses resulting from a violation of Chapter 1345. of the Revised Code and does not include damages for noneconomic loss as defined in section 2315.18 of the Revised Code.\n\n(H) Nothing in this section shall preclude a consumer from also proceeding with a cause of action under any other theory of law.",
